Well, I don't think omega is that buggy anymore, but it still stinks.
In his haste to add lots of neat features, Brothers has totally
neglected to adjust game balance.  As a result, omega is wildly
erratic, requiring almost constant character backups.  It's possible
to find an object of near game-winning power one turn, and be killed
by some random event (for example, acid traps have a pretty good
chance of killing you outright if you're carrying any magical objects)
two turns later.  There is very little element of tactics or skill in
omega. 

